Encoding function:
```ts
function encodeLatin1(s: string): Uint8Array {
  const out = new Uint8Array(s.length)
  for (let i=0;i<s.length;i++) out[i] = s.charCodeAt(i) & 0xff
  return out
}
```
But if there are code points > 0xFF, charCodeAt gives e.g. 0x4E2D, & 0xff = 0x2D which silently corrupts. So we must only allow when all representable or replaceMode. Since we block download unless representable/replaced, and outputText replaces unrepresentable with '?' when replaceMode, the encode is safe. But to be robust, encodeLatin1 should itself map non-representable to 0x3F ('?') rather than truncate. Let me implement:
```ts
function encodeLatin1(s: string, replace: boolean): Uint8Array {
  const out = new Uint8Array(s.length)
  for (let i=0;i<s.length;i++){
    const c = s.charCodeAt(i)
    if (c <= 0xff) out[i]=c
    else out[i]= replace ? 0x3f : 0x3f // but we shouldn't reach without replace
  }
}
```
Better: for code points, astral chars are surrogate pairs (2 code units); replacing each surrogate with '?' yields two '?' (one per unit). Hmm, that's ugly. We should replace the whole code point with a single '?'. Let me build outputText by iterating code points:
```ts
function replaceUnrepresentable(s: string): string {
  let out=''
  for (const ch of s) {
    const cp = ch.codePointAt(0)!
    out += cp <= 0xff ? ch : '?'
  }
  return out
}
```
That replaces each astral code point with one '?'. Then encodeLatin1 can simply map charCodeAt & 0xff, which for BMP chars <=0xff is correct, and all unrepresentable are gone. Good.

But note: for BMP chars > 0xFF, `for...of` yields the char; replaced with '?'. Good.

Now position detection: line/col based on original text (convertedText before replacement) using code points. Implement:
```ts
function scanUnrepresentable(s: string) {
  const list = []
  let line=1, col=0
  for (const ch of s) {
    const cp = ch.codePointAt(0)!
    if (ch === '\n') { line++; col=0; continue }
    col++
    if (cp > 0xff) list.push({ line, col, char: ch, cp, kind: kindOf(cp) })
  }
  return list
}
```
Handle \r\n: col increments for \r then \n resets. Minor. Since we scan convertedText after normalizeNewlines (which keeps CRLF if mode keep). Fine; \r is <=0xff so ignored, col counts it. Acceptable.

kindOf(cp): 
- if cp >= 0x1F000 || (cp>=0x2600 && cp<=0x27BF) → 'emoji'
- if cp >= 0x4E00 && cp <= 0x9FFF → '汉字'
- if cp >= 0x3000 && cp <= 0x303F → '中文标点'
- if cp >= 0xFF00 && cp <= 0xFFEF → '全角字符'
- else '符号/字符'

